our world is constantly changing many  scenes in our everyday lives that are  seemingly static in fact contain subtle  variations and changes that are  invisible to us imagine you had special  glasses that allowed you to see subtle  changes that cannot be seen with the  naked eye like small variations in the  color of the skin has blood pulsates  through it or the subtle breathing  motions of a baby these changes are  hidden in ordinary videos we capture  with our cameras and smartphones given  an input video for each pixel we analyze  the color variation over time and  amplify this variation which gives us a  magnified version of video  in this example the pulse signal is  amplified 100 times  we can also analyze the frequencies of  this signal and extract the heart rate  this doesn't require attaching any  sensors to the patient and the accuracy  is comparable with hospital grade  monitors  the same algorithm can also reveal  imperceptible motions like the pulsing  motions of arteries in the wrist  when a person fixates at a point the IMA  move from subtle head motions or from  involuntary eye movements known as  microseconds such motions are very hard  to notice even in this close-up shot of  the eye but become apparent when  amplified 150 times invisible motions  are also created by mechanical parts  such as the shutter and flipping mirror  in a DSLR camera that produce tiny  motions when taking pictures  structures are designed to sway in the  wind but their motion 2 is often  invisible amplifying the changes in this  video reveals the swaying of the cranes  mast and the undulation of its hook  you
 

